  "id": "COMPOUND:41033 - PROTEIN:5780",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between the compound [(E)-2-[(1S,5S,7R,8S,11S)-11-(2-methoxypropan-2-yl)-8-methyl-5-(2-oxopropyl)-4-oxatricyclo[6.3.1.02,6]dodec-2(6)-en-7-yl]ethenyl] 3-methylbut-2-enoate and SQ20B, through a series of target interactions. The compound is identified as a target of multiple dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family members, which are known to act as enzymes involved in the metabolism of various substrates. These SDRs are further targeted by additional compounds, including 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and 6-Hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone, both of which are also targets of SQ20B. This indicates that the compound may exert its effects through a pathway involving the SDR family, potentially by modulating the activity of these enzymes. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a substrate or inhibitor of these SDRs, which in turn could influence the activity of SQ20B. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that the compound interacts with SQ20B via a mechanism involving the SDR family, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
